rewritten-to-match
Same maze, same generate() in prepare. The reference's BinaryHeap<Reverse<(i32, usize)>> is a binary min-heap in two arrays ordered by (f, cell index) (4,096 slots; it reaches 31 for the run parameters, measured by simulating it); every pair is pushed at most once, so any correct heap pops the same sequence. The came-from, g and best-f arrays are filled each run as the reference allocates them. As in the BFS the path's length and middle cell are taken from the chain of parents. Other stores are checked and undo-logged. Scratch state rebuilt every run (the reference's locals: came, gs, bf, hf, hv) is declared `unlogged`, kept out of the undo log.
